From the above datasets, the data was split into train-test fractions in an 80:20 ratio. Given the large number of input features, we identified the top 200 genes (hereafter referred to as highly-correlated genes or HCGs) with the highest Spearman correlation with either of the output variables in the training data alone. We also included the target gene if it is not within the HCG set. This subset of gene expression values scaled through Z-transformations constituted the training feature set \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
